{
  "requirement": "The bundled skills MUST direct agents to make a requirement distributed only when its obligation applies on its own at each of many sites, such as a convention every validation function follows; to use `{impl}` instead when particular code carries out the requirement as a whole; and to mark with `{impl}` the code that carries out any obligation of a distributed requirement that its sites do not uphold.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject requires the bundled skills to direct agents on three points. (1) Make a requirement distributed only when its obligation applies on its own at each of many sites. (2) Use `{impl}` when particular code carries out the requirement as a whole. (3) Mark with `{impl}` the code that carries out any obligation of a distributed requirement that its sites do not uphold.\n\nThe single test, `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_make_a_requirement_distributed_only_for_per_site_obligations]`, is the right kind of check for a guidance-text requirement. It extracts the `## Do` section of the habeas skill's `references/distributed-requirements.md`. That is the home of this guidance, and the other skills only refer to it, as `fn[bundled_skills_refer_to_a_topic_home_instead_of_restating_it]` shows. It then asserts with `assert_text` that the collapsed section contains two exact phrases:\n\n- \"Make a requirement distributed only when its obligation applies on its own at each site; when particular code carries out the requirement as a whole, use `{impl}` there.\" This covers obligations 1 and 2.\n- \"Separate obligations each site upholds from obligations particular code carries out, and mark that code `{impl}`.\" This covers obligation 3.\n\nThe helpers `section`, `assert_text` and `distributed_reference` are reached from the marked test. `section` stops at the next same-level or higher heading outside code fences, so the assertions are scoped to the Do list. `assert_text` fails if a phrase is missing. I read the reference's Do paragraph, and the Don't paragraph restates obligation 3 for sites that carry out other obligations. The \"such as a convention every validation function follows\" wording is only an illustration and needs no separate assertion.\n\nThe test would fail if any of the three directions were removed or reworded away. I found no unchecked obligation, no wrong expected result and no applicable fixme.",
  "references": "78662a5f93bdc1cce2c30f2a56821845f344b48e61610e0248463e30f52ffe47",
